    {
      "id": "14817",
      "body": "Multi-category filtering — recommended approach pls let me know your thoughts since this is custom\nUser:557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8 User:60084df92b411b0076ad73d6\n![\"image-20260918-024343.png\"](image-20260918-024343.png)\nThe SFCC Search API only accepts a single category (cgid) per request. To support filtering by multiple categories simultaneously, the solution uses a custom product refinement attribute rather than a custom API:\n \n---\n \nBackend (Integration team)\n \n1. Define a custom product attribute — e.g. c\\_categoryIds — on each product that stores all category IDs the product belongs to (populated via catalog feed or import script)\n1. Configure the SFCC Search profile in Business Manager to index c\\_categoryIds as a searchable refinement attribute\n1. Products become queryable by category membership through the standard refinement API\n \n---\n \nFrontend (our side)\n \nWhen the shopper selects multiple sibling categories (e.g. Jackets  Bottoms  Knitwear), apply them as a single pipe-separated refinement:\n \n/category/clothing?refine=c\\_categoryIds%3Djackets%7Cbottoms%7Cknitwear\n \nThe | pipe is SFCC's native OR separator within a refinement — the API returns products that belong to any of the selected categories. No custom endpoint, no workaround — it's the same refinement mechanism used for Colour and Size.\n \nThe filter drawer category section becomes a multi-select checkbox group that builds this refinement, and the page-level chip strip treats c\\_categoryIds exactly like any other applied refinement (one chip per value, removable individually).",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Bryan Ian De Vera",
        "name": "Bryan Ian De Vera",
        "email": "bryan.ian.de.vera@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/26a1772cba36a20826bfadc61d11fd68?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBV-3.png"
      },
      "created": "2026-09-18T12:44:16.372+1000",
      "updated": "2026-09-18T12:44:16.372+1000"
    }
  ]
}"}

